{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/node.go | sed -n '205,242p;334,346p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/raft.go | sed -n '1539,1548p;2123,2158p'; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nfor x in s['selections']:\n if x.get('operation_id')=='e2ef03c8e73646f7b7031abbd63be3df':print(json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"  1539\t\t\t\t\t\tpr.Inflights.FreeLE(m.Index)\n  1540\t\t\t\t\t}\n  1541\t\n  1542\t\t\t\t\tif r.maybeCommit() {\n  1543\t\t\t\t\t\t// committed index has progressed for the term, so it is safe\n  1544\t\t\t\t\t\t// to respond to pending read index requests\n  1545\t\t\t\t\t\treleasePendingReadIndexMessages(r)\n  1546\t\t\t\t\t\tr.bcastAppend()\n  1547\t\t\t\t\t} else if r.id != m.From && pr.CanBumpCommit(r.raftLog.committed) {\n  1548\t\t\t\t\t\t// This node may be missing the latest commit index, so send it.\n  2123\tfunc releasePendingReadIndexMessages(r *raft) {\n  2124\t\tif len(r.pendingReadIndexMessages) == 0 {\n  2125\t\t\t// Fast path for the common case to avoid a call to storage.LastIndex()\n  2126\t\t\t// via committedEntryInCurrentTerm.\n  2127\t\t\treturn\n  2128\t\t}\n  2129\t\tif !r.committedEntryInCurrentTerm() {\n  2130\t\t\tr.logger.Error(\"pending MsgReadIndex should be released only after first commit in current term\")\n  2131\t\t\treturn\n  2132\t\t}\n  2133\t\n  2134\t\tmsgs := r.pendingReadIndexMessages\n  2135\t\tr.pendingReadIndexMessages = nil\n  2136\t\n  2137\t\tfor _, m := range msgs {\n  2138\t\t\tsendMsgReadIndexResponse(r, m)\n  2139\t\t}\n  2140\t}\n  2141\t\n  2142\tfunc sendMsgReadIndexResponse(r *raft, m pb.Message) {\n  2143\t\t// thinking: use an internally defined context instead of the user given context.\n  2144\t\t// We can express this in terms of the term and index instead of a user-supplied value.\n  2145\t\t// This would allow multiple reads to piggyback on the same message.\n  2146\t\tswitch r.readOnly.option {\n  2147\t\t// If more than the local vote is needed, go through a full broadcast.\n  2148\t\tcase ReadOnlySafe:\n  2149\t\t\tr.readOnly.addRequest(r.raftLog.committed, m)\n  2150\t\t\t// The local node automatically acks the request.\n  2151\t\t\tr.readOnly.recvAck(r.id, m.Entries[0].Data)\n  2152\t\t\tr.bcastHeartbeatWithCtx(m.Entries[0].Data)\n  2153\t\tcase ReadOnlyLeaseBased:\n  2154\t\t\tif resp := r.responseToReadIndexReq(m, r.raftLog.committed); resp.To != None {\n  2155\t\t\t\tr.send(resp)\n  2156\t\t\t}\n  2157\t\t}\n  2158\t}\n{\n  \"operation_id\": \"e2ef03c8e73646f7b7031abbd63be3df\",\n  \"action\": \"explore\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The public synchronous Node contract permits early Advance; execute the actual election, delayed configuration activation and read paths to discriminate reachability before fixing a liveness obligation.\",\n  \"feedback\": {\n    \"ref_ids\": [\n      \"node-early-advance\",\n      \"doc-early-advance\",\n      \"campaign\",\n      \"config-activate\",\n      \"pending-read-intent\"\n    ],\n    \"answered\": \"The exploration uses Node directly, so the early-Advance scheduling premise comes from that entry interface. It persists all Ready state before advancing, holds application batches only on the prospective leader in FIFO order, drives a real new election, and holds only selected append network messages to separate old and new quorum thresholds. Status and ReadState are the observed endpoints; no private protocol state is assigned or read concurrently.\",\n    \"remaining\": [\n      \"Actual execution must establish whether the proposed prefix and trigger are reachable.\",\n      \"If the original read remains pending, determine the exact bounded release responsibility and preserve the distinction from a timeout-based liveness conclusion.\"\n    ],\n    \"understanding\": null,\n    \"rationale\": \"Actual production and same-history correlation are the limiting premises. A later independent read and an additional real proposal are controls that can distinguish absent quorum communication from a pending-release path.\",\n    \"question_updates\": {}\n  },\n  \"map_updated\": false,\n  \"map_changes\": {},\n  \"accepted_versions\": {\n    \"audit_spec\": 2,\n    \"units\": {},\n    \"artifacts\": {}\n  },\n  \"candidate_ids\": []\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_read_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim='C-first-commit-read-release'; binding='D-read-release'\ng=dict(source_ids=['leader-admit','leader-match','read-pending','config-activate'],expectation_ids=['pending-read-intent'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='pending-read-intent describes this particular internal queue as holding reads that cannot be answered before a new leader commits in its term, and says they will be handled as fast as the first log is committed in that term. Interpret this as a local transition responsibility: after the first-current-term commitment transition completes, a request already held solely on that condition must be released from this waiting queue for ordinary read processing. The expectation is attributed to that specific implementation statement, not inferred solely from differing call sites. Public ReadIndex explicitly allows requests to be lost and requires retry; this is not a claim of unconditional read completion, linearizability violation or an elapsed-time deadline.',applicability='Synchronous public Node, ReadOnlySafe, surviving leader and unique request context, real pending request before first-current-term commit. Membership activation or an append reply can establish that commit condition. Early Advance is permitted by the Node and doc.go interface statements, with Ready application order retained.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Public read completion can require retries; a missing ReadState alone would not violate this local queue-release proposition.','The append-reply path explicitly releases this queue; membership activation must be examined separately.'])\nq=dict(question='Does the pending-read consumer release a request waiting for the first current-term commit when that commit is established by application-activated membership, under the synchronous Node early-Advance contract?',importance='A retained request can depend on an unrelated future proposal despite the commit precondition being satisfied. This is an implementation progress-contract question; it does not itself imply unsafe reads or a public guarantee that ReadIndex never drops requests.',source_ids=['pending-read-intent','read-api-contract','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance'],participants=['Synchronous Node leader','Application applying a delayed committed configuration','Voting peers'],objects=['Committed prefix','Unique pending ReadIndex request','Application-activated voter set'],contexts=['Synchronous early Advance before configuration activation, preserving Ready application order','Same leader term across the selected request and commit transition','ReadOnlySafe'],event_paths=['Node.ReadIndex -> stepLeader pendingReadIndexMessages -> Node.ApplyConfChange -> switchToConfig -> maybeCommit -> inspect pending queue after Stop barrier','Control: actual MsgAppResp first advances commit and invokes releasePendingReadIndexMessages'],activity_classes=['A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B-read','B-aggregate'],fact_ids=['F-committed'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-entry':'Documents and implements early Advance and serialized Node ownership.','B-campaign':'Election guard reads reported applied; early Advance makes its boundary relevant.','B-membership':'Application activates a changed majority and invokes commitment recomputation.','B-election-result':'Actual vote messages establish the new leader.','B-apply':'Advance reports application progress before deferred work finishes under the synchronous permission.','B-storage-release':'Persistence precedes release of all synchronous Ready messages in the driver.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Public ReadIndex may be lost without notice and callers must retry; no unconditional external completion guarantee is asserted.','hasUnappliedConfChanges blocks a campaign with committed configuration changes above reported applied; the driver uses the documented early-Advance permission rather than assigning applied directly.','Ordinary append-response commitment invokes releasePendingReadIndexMessages.','Source exploration showed later read processing and an additional proposal can release the original request; this is not evidence of permanent loss.'],unknowns=['Will a formal correlated observation show the same request still in the first-commit waiting queue after a completed membership-triggered current-term commit, versus its removal on the ordinary append-reply path?'],priority=1,trigger_rationale='Exploration 680ffdc882db43e0931033ebfd08b3de established the actual public-Node prefix and commitment transition, but is not property evidence. A stopped-owner observation can directly measure queue membership at this local endpoint, avoiding timeout-based liveness claims and concurrent private-state access.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v2.json'));refs=set(q['source_ids'])\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids']:refs.update(b['source_ids'])\nfor f in m['facts']:\n if f['id'] in q['fact_ids']:refs.update(f['source_ids'])\nq['source_ids']=sorted(refs)\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For a leader request already queued solely awaiting the first committed log entry in its current term, completion of the local transition that establishes that commit condition must release the request from pendingReadIndexMessages for ordinary read processing; a separate later proposal must not be required to discharge this queue condition.',source_ids=['pending-read-intent','read-api-contract','read-pending','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance'],scope=dict(description='Local first-current-term-commit waiting-queue release under synchronous Node early Advance, with unchanged leadership during request and trigger.',assumptions=['ReadOnlySafe and unique request context.','Committed configuration application retains Ready order despite early Advance.','Non-Byzantine peers and successful persistent-storage completion represented by MemoryStorage.'],excluded=['Unconditional public ReadIndex completion or service deadlines','Consensus safety or linearizability violation','Physical crash durability','Asynchronous storage mode and malformed messages'],parameters={'async_storage_writes':False,'read_mode':'ReadOnlySafe','application':'documented early Advance with ordered delayed configuration activation'}),pending=[],grounding=g)\nb=dict(id=binding,material_id='read-pending',symbol='releasePendingReadIndexMessages',start_line=2123,end_line=2140,description='Ordinary consumer removes pre-current-term pending requests and initiates their read-mode processing once current-term commitment is established.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['pending-read-intent','leader-match','config-activate','read-pending'],rationale='The queue expectation is explicit; this helper performs the transition. Compare its append-reply caller with membership-triggered commitment.')])\nleg=dict(source_ids=['node-start-and-restart','node-step-and-read','node-control-methods','node-loop','node-stop','doc-early-advance','node-early-advance','bootstrap-contract','storage-memory','storage-snap-append','campaign','candidate-follower','config-activate','read-pending','read-api-contract'],expectation_ids=['doc-early-advance','node-early-advance','conf-contract','read-api-contract'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='Four Nodes start with identical Bootstrap peers and consume actual Ready batches. Each Ready writes Entries and HardState before messages or Advance. Node 2 temporarily defers every application batch in order but advances after persistence, as explicitly permitted by synchronous Node/doc.go. A real committed removal entry is later applied in that same FIFO batch order. Campaign and actual vote replies elect Node 2; only its append network messages to peers 1 and 4 are held, preserving an active quorum of the subsequent three-voter configuration through nodes 2 and 3. The original read is submitted locally while commitment is still from the previous term; Status serializes after ReadIndex reception. The experiment case then applies the delayed config; the control first releases actual held append messages so old-config quorum commits through the ordinary response path, then applies all delayed batches. After ApplyConfChange returns and Status observes commit, Stop waits for the Node owner to terminate, and only then the harness reads its private queue without mutation or races. Stop does not clear that queue. There are no tick timeouts in the selected transition. Each observation finishes at the local queue-release endpoint, not a completed client read.',applicability='Two independent real histories differing only in which actual event first commits the new-term entry. Post-stop no progress is expected. Timing waits only let Ready channels run; they are not an oracle. MemoryStorage models successful stable writes in a no-crash schedule.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Using private raft methods to assign leadership or commit would not establish this legal public-Node history; none are used.','The stopped-owner queue observation answers local release, while actual read service remains outside scope.'])\nplan=dict(description='Run configuration-first and append-reply-first histories with public synchronous Nodes. Observe the original request identity, leader and old commit term before the trigger. After the configuration API returns, observe current-term commitment and inspect whether that same request remains in the first-commit queue after a Stop ownership barrier.',claim_id=claim,binding_ids=[binding],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Actual four-node election and committed membership reduction, documented early Advance, two trigger orders, then stopped-owner queue inspection.',semantic_changes=['No target changes or private state assignments.','Same-package queue read occurs only after public Stop returns; stopping ends the observation independently of the forbidden queue state.','Normal application is a no-op except required ApplyConfChange; no external client result is modeled.','MemoryStorage represents successful storage completion.','current_term_committed is derived from the stored term at observed committed index compared with observed current term; raw operands are emitted.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='read',event='read_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='read_call_returned',value=True),dict(field='leader_state',value='StateLeader'),dict(field='commit_term_before',op='ne',reference='leader_term')])],legality=leg),monitors=[dict(id='M-first-commit-read-release',checker_id='first-commit-read-release',event='release_observed',binding_ids=[binding],grounding=g,admission_alias='read',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='first-commit-read-release',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='transition_returned',value=True),antecedent=dict(field='current_term_committed',value=True),assertion=dict(field='waiting_for_first_commit',value=False),identity_fields=['operation_id','request','leader','leader_term'],description='For the admitted request in the same leader term, a completed local transition with a current-term committed entry implies the request no longer waits in the pre-first-commit pending queue. This does not require ReadState output or public read completion.')],uncertainties=['The local release expectation is attributed to the internal queue comment. Public ReadIndex explicitly allows loss and retries, so this must not be described as an unconditional public completion guarantee.','The same-history construction exercises one documented synchronous scheduling permission and two trigger orders, not all configurations or application strategies.'])\n# A comparison reference names a field in its ow